          skills21stCentury: "Communication and collaboration skills: Understand and accept other people's perspectives. Able to follow a speaker and create their own meaning, probing questions to check and deepen their own understanding. Able to follow and take part in a group discussion and express opinions when called upon. Apply knowledge to real life situations by examining evidence to solve problems. Able to identify and analyse different points of view they hear in a discussion and explain how they are different. Can convey simple ideas or thoughts to a wider group, for example in a group discussion.\n\nDigital literacy: Can confidently prepare presentation using ICT and respecting other people's privacy. Share information among team members using social media ethically. Ability to search and share digital information. Ability to type presentations and reports.\n\nCreativity and innovation: Ability to combine ideas and concepts to make new ones. Can merge simple ideas to create new ones and identify those ideas have different components.\n\nPersonal development and Leadership skills: Able to articulate and explain one's feelings in a group situation and working with others.\n\n(For LO.2 & LO.3) Critical Thinking and Problem-solving skills: Think rationally and clearly to solve problems. Use open and closed questions to construct a conclusion or ending.",
          gesiSelValues: "GESI: Learners having experienced a teaching approach that ensures gender equality and social inclusion, where they work with each other in an inclusive way; cross-sharing knowledge and understanding among groups and individuals lead them to:\n  Respect individuals of different backgrounds.\n  Embrace diversity and practice inclusion.\n  Examine and dispel misconceptions/myths in clothing selection.\n  Interrogate their stereotypes and biases about gender and the role men, women and people with special needs play in the selection and production of clothing items.\n\nSEL: Learners having been given the opportunity to experience varied teaching approaches in an enabling environment will be equipped with social emotional learning skills to:\n  Participate in decision-making related to classroom activities and rules.\n  Explore and apply different skills in clothing construction.\n  Offer positive support to each other.\n\nNational Values:\n  Tolerance\n  Friendliness\n  Open mindedness\n  Patience\n  Hard work\n  Humility, etc.",
