          gesiSelValues: "GESI: Learners having experienced a teaching approach that ensures gender equality and social inclusion, where they work with each other in an inclusive way; cross sharing knowledge and understanding among groups and individuals lead them to:\n  Respect individuals of different backgrounds.\n  Embrace diversity and practice inclusion.\n  Examine and dispel misconceptions/ myths about gender as they relate clothing selection, care and maintenance.\n  Interrogate their stereotypes and biases about gender and the role men, women and special needs people play in clothing selection, care and maintenance.\n  Identify injustice, especially in recognition of the contributions of different groups and individuals to the effective management and maintenance of clothing.\n\nSEL: Learners having been given the opportunity to experience varied teaching approaches in an enabling environment will be equipped with social emotional learning skills to:\n  Build self-confidence.\n  Practice and identify how others may be feeling about their choice of clothing.\n  Reflect on positive and negative consequences of their choice of clothing for occasions.\n\nNational Values:\n  Tolerance\n  Friendliness\n  Open mindedness\n  Patience\n  Hard work\n  Humility, etc.",
