                  exemplar: "In friendship/mixed ability/gender groups, use talking point strategies to discuss the concept of renovation and remodelling in clothing production.\nE.g.\nRenovation: it is making minor changes in the appearance of clothing to renew them.\nRemodelling: making a different article out of an existing one, etc.\n\nGroup Work:\nIn mixed ability/gender groups, use videos/pictures/realia of customized clothing/surf the internet to examine the importance of renovating and remodelling of articles.\n\nStructured talk for learning Approaches: With the aid of videos, charts, slides or posters, discuss the importance of renovating and remodelling articles.\nE.g.\n        Environmental impact and sustainability\n        Financial gains\n        Conserving sentimental and cultural Value\n        Individualisation and creative expression\n        Resource management\n        Fashion trends, etc.\n\nGroup work/Collaborative learning Approaches: In mixed ability groups, use talking point/ pyramid discussion/panel discussion to examine the importance of renovating and remodelling articles.\n\nExperiential learning:\nIn mixed ability/gender cultural/friendship groups, organise a visit to sewing shops/centres within the community to observe how articles are renovated and remodelled.",
